# Archon inner-repo excludes — managed by InnerGit._write_default_excludes
# .archon/ tracking is handled by _stage_all (git add -f), not here:
# outer .gitignore's `.archon/` rule wins over info/exclude, so any
# `!.archon/` negation at this level would be silently ignored.
# Build artifacts and OS junk.
.lake/
lake-packages/
.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.git/
# Multi-lane worktrees live under .archon/lanes/<id>/ — each is its
# own checkout sharing this same git-dir; the parent worktree must
# not stage them or 'git add' would recurse into nested checkouts.
.archon/lanes/
# Secret env files anywhere in the worktree — provider keys, OAuth
# tokens, DB passwords. The loop loads these via load_env_file() at
# startup; they must not flow through inner-git time-travel either.
# Note: `_stage_all` ALSO skips these by name when force-adding
# `.archon/` children, since `git add -f` bypasses info/exclude.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Auto-generated lane provider settings ({"env": {ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, …}})
# materialize per-iteration in this directory. They embed API keys —
# never commit them. The lane runtime regenerates them at the start
# of each multilane round, so dropping them on disk is fine.
.archon/multilane/lanes/
